==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PermissionMatrix removes the closed-world assignment of allowed cells, freeing the PermMatrix.Allowed relation to contain any Role->OperationKind pairs. The injection then forces a forbidden cell into the Allowed set, directly violating LeastPrivilege and PermissionGrounding.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PermissionGrounding, FR_002_CustomerPermissions, FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - PermissionGrounding: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_002_CustomerPermissions: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OneInFlightPerCustomer removes the constraint that prevents a customer from having two simultaneous in-flight applications. The injection forces two distinct applications with the same customer to both be in-flight, producing the exact counterexample FR-008 was designed to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer: PASS (vacuous?)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionByAssignedOfficer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecisionByAssignedOfficer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_DecisionByAssignedOfficer removes the structural constraint binding a Decision's decidedBy to the application's assignedOfficer. The injection forces a Decision where the deciding user is different from the assigned officer, directly violating FR-013.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides, AttributionCorrectness
      - FR_013_OnlyAssignedOfficerDecides: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditNoDuplicateTransitions  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditNoDuplicateTransitions.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditNoDuplicateTransitions removes the append-only guard that prevents duplicate (previousStatus, newStatus) pairs for the same application. The injection forces two audit entries on the same application with identical transition fields, violating the append-only and exactly-one-per-transition invariants.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_018_019_AuditTrailIntegrity, FR_019_ExactlyOneAuditEntryPerTransition
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_018_019_AuditTrailIntegrity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_ExactlyOneAuditEntryPerTransition: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditValidTransitions  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditValidTransitions.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditValidTransitions removes the constraint that limits audit entries to the four documented transitions. The injection introduces an audit entry recording a transition out of a terminal state (Approved→Rejected), which represents the exact immutability violation FR-016 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_016_TerminalStateImmutable, FR_StateTransitionValidity
      - FR_016_TerminalStateImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_StateTransitionValidity: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditSubmitActorIsCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditSubmitActorIsCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditSubmitActorIsCustomer allows the initial audit entry's actor to be a non-customer user. The injection forces an initial submission entry (no previousStatus) where the actor is a LoanOfficer, violating attribution correctness and the invariant that only the owning customer can appear as actor on the submission event.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_020_CustomerSeesOwnAppsOnly, NoInformationLeakage
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_020_CustomerSeesOwnAppsOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

